# Hydri Implementation Proof

After any task that implements or fixes behavior, close with **Captain closeout** (user-facing, short, decisive) then `HYDRI_IMPLEMENTATION_PROOF` (technical). Do not claim "done" or "it works" without both. **Do not lead the close with technical proof.**

Plan/audit-only: Captain closeout with 🟡 Segue com cuidado is enough — omit full proof block.

Full spec: `docs/agents/AGENTS-IMPLEMENTATION-PROOF.md`

## Captain closeout (required first in closing section)

Written for the user, not another agent. No jargon when a human phrase works.

```md
## Captain closeout

🟢/🟡/🔴 [Decisão curta]

Em humano:
[1 a 3 frases curtas sem jargão]

Prova simples:
[1 linha em linguagem simples]

Falta provar:
[1 linha objetiva]

Próxima ação:
[1 ação clara]
```

| Emoji | Decisão | Maps to **Result** |
|-------|---------|-------------------|
| 🟢 | Pode seguir | Worked |
| 🟡 | Segue com cuidado | Partial |
| 🔴 | Para agora | Did not work |

Optional **Detalhes técnicos** after Captain closeout for paths, commands, components, proof levels.

## HYDRI_IMPLEMENTATION_PROOF fields (technical)

1. **Result:** Worked | Partial | Did not work
2. Change implemented
3. Objective evidence
4. Commands run
5. Tests affected
6. Preview / manual QA (when applicable)
7. **Mobile viewport coverage** (required for UI categories)
8. **Operation Zero Redemoinho proof fields** (required for implementation): pattern reuse, token, magic number, i18n, kebab-case, sass module, dead code/docs, feature/shared, mock/domain, persona/value, CWV/cognitive cost, tests/lab cost — see `docs/agents/AGENTS-IMPLEMENTATION-PROOF.md`
9. Files changed
10. Not validated
11. Remaining risks
12. Why the implementation may still be wrong
13. Recommended next action

## Cannot claim success when

- Mandatory validation was not run (`npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run check:i18n`)
- Operation Zero Redemoinho proof fields skipped on implementation
- New hardcoded UI string, token outside `--hy-*`, or path outside kebab-case
- Affected route or component was not inspected
- Tests only assert fragile text/class contracts
- UI changed without visual/runtime preview
- Mobile UI closed with 🟢 after testing only one width (must be 🟡 Partial)
- Behavior changed without test or manual QA
- Errors were waved off as "out of scope" without evidence

## Proof levels (report highest achieved)

- **P0:** lint, typecheck, i18n check
- **P1:** affected unit/integration tests
- **P2:** local preview / manual QA
- **P3:** CI / PR green
- **P4:** user sign-off or screenshot/video

## Quick checklists

**Mobile UI:** three widths (small 320×568 or 360×740, standard 390×844, large 430×932); nav/sheets/cards/chips/search/controls checks; width-dependent behavior when layout mutates; screenshot per width when used; light mode; initial state; primary interaction; close/cancel; scroll; safe-area/BottomNav; no desktop regression when mobile-only. Captain closeout: "Testado em celular pequeno, médio e grande." or "Só testado em um tamanho, precisa revisar responsividade."

**i18n / routes:** `/[locale]`, locales when copy changes, no new hardcoded strings, `npm run check:i18n`.

**CSS:** CSS/Sass Modules only, no `globals.scss` for features, no `!important`; prefer `.module.sass` for new/touched component styles; kebab-case for new/touched paths.

**UI architecture:** dumb components, logic in hooks, data separated in scope; read `.cursor/rules/hydri-ui-architecture.mdc` before UI work.

Default mobile preview: `/pt-BR/cargas`.
